# Git Workflow

## Commits
- Format: `<type>: <imperative>` (feat/fix/refactor/docs/test/chore/perf/ci).
- Subject ≤72 chars, imperative mood. One logical change per commit.
- Body explains *why*, not *what*.

## Branching (GitHub Flow)
- `main` always deployable. Short-lived feature branches (1–3 days).
- PR → review → CI green → merge → deploy.

## PRs
- Title ≤70 chars; detail in body.
- Summary = *why* bullets. Include test-plan checklist.
- Base decisions on full `git diff <base>...HEAD`, not just latest commit.

## Hygiene
- Never commit secrets or `.env`. Never force-push `main`. Never skip hooks.
- Prefer new commits over `--amend` once pushed.
